  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When salicylic acid is heated with methyl alcohol, the carboxyl group of salicylic acid is esterified producing a strong-smelling liquid ester (methyl salicylate). Aspirin is prepared by chemical synthesis from salicylic acid, through acetylation with acetic anhydride.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0018_03122118f4d4.png\" style=\"width: 602px; height: 150px;\" />&nbsp;Hence, reagent&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively are:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>CO</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>.</p>"
